# Own summons walk-through (server/README.md "Summons: targets, walk-through, levels"). Owner report 2026-10-21: "the Necromancer's risen
# warriors block the way": a melee minion stands next to its owner in a corridor and the owner could only push it
# (pushable monsters move one tile per push). A player now walks through its OWN summons: Player::canWalkthrough (the
# server's step and path check, Tile::queryAdd) and Player::canWalkthroughEx (the creature packets' "unpassable" byte,
# so the client predicts the step through, Tile::isWalkable honours Creature::isPassable; no client patch). Nobody
# else does: another player's or a party member's summons still block (body blocks in PvP are unchanged), the summon
# itself still needs a free tile to move to, and every other blocking rule of the tile (walls, items, other creatures,
# protection zones, floor changes) stays. Lua's setMaster runs after Game.createMonster placed the monster, so
# Game::updateCreatureType (called by setMaster) now also sends the walk-through state (Game::updateCreatureWalkthrough).
# Applies after 0001-0054.
--- a/src/game.cpp
